joe Linux: a privileged bash runs and sources only sealed script files.

Before reading a script file (one named on the command line, or one read by
`source`, `.` or as a startup file) bash asks the joe security module whether
the file is sealed. Commands typed interactively and `-c` strings are not
files and are not affected. See packages/linux/joe-lsm/joe.c.

